                <pb facs="0843" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4474: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-19T20:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1922—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 20—5:41
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>271. My 267, June 17, 1 p.m.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d488-f1"/> Canton 16th and
                    17th, Sun with three gunboats raked bund with machine gun and rapid fire. Two
                    American buildings hit. Consul 18th protested to Sun at Whampoa and Sun replied
                    would again bombard but not bund unless fired on.</p>
                <p>Chen in Waichow and will remain there for the present. His nephew told consul two
                    gunboats willing to come over, also said forces sent to Shiuchow prevent troops
                    in Kiating [<hi rendition="#italic">Kiangsi?</hi>] coming to rescue.</p>
                <p>Have advised Admiral by wireless that American citizens and property may need
                    protection.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
